/**
 * Changes the delivery settings of the current cooperative. Requires `SETTINGS_MANAGE`. Each top-level field is
 * optional and a field left out keeps its value, so the mailbox form and the bot form save separately:
 *
 * - `email` present replaces every mailbox field (a field absent or empty in it is cleared), except the
 *   password: an absent or empty `password` keeps the saved one. Clearing `user` (no sign-in to the server)
 *   also removes the saved password.
 * - `telegram.botToken` absent or empty keeps the saved token. A new token is saved sealed, its last four
 *   characters are shown from then on, the bot's @name is forgotten until the next `testDeliveryTelegram`, and
 *   the bot of the cooperative restarts with it.
 * - `emailRatePerSecond` (letters a second, 1 to 10) and `notifyPayments` change only when present.
 *
 * A change is written to the audit log as `DELIVERY_SETTINGS_CHANGED` (entity type `DELIVERY_SETTINGS`, label
 * `delivery-settings`) with the old and the new value of every changed field (`host`, `port`, `security`,
 * `user`, `fromAddress`, `fromName`, `emailRatePerSecond`, `notifyPayments`); a changed secret is listed as the
 * field `password` or `botToken` with neither value, so the history shows only that it changed. Saving the
 * current values writes nothing. 400 `VALIDATION_FAILED` for a value outside its limits.
 * @summary Change the cooperative's mailbox and bot
 */
